<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="cila17.1"> 
<l>kayaleḻutiya vimaya neṟṟiyiṉ</l>
<l>ayaleḻutiya puliyum villum</l>
<l>nāvalan taṇpoḻiṉ maṉṉar</l>
<l>ēval kēṭpap pārara cāṇṭa</l>
<l>mālai veṇkuṭaip pāṇṭiyaṉ kōyiliṟ</l>
<l>kālai muracaṅ kaṉaikura liyampumākaliṉ</l>
<l>neymmuṟainamak kiṉṟāmeṉ</l>
<l>ṟaiyaitaṉ makaḷaikkūuyk</l>
<l>kaṭaikayiṟu mattuṅkoṇ</l>
<l>ṭiṭaimutumakaḷ vantutōṉṟumaṉ</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
<l>Because the intense sound of the morning Muracam drum</l>
<l>Sounded at the palace of the Pāṇṭiyaṉ [with] a garland and a parasol</l>
 <l> Who ruled [his] wide kingdom; so that [even] the kings [of] the cool groves</l>
<l>Of Nāvalam; [and] the tiger [= Cōḻas] and the bow [= Cēras]</l>
<l>Who marked [their signs] on the forehead of the Himalayas</l>
<l>Beside [= secondary to] the carp [= the Pāṇṭiya symbol];</l>
<l>[All] listen to [the Pāṇṭiyaṉ’s] command,</l>
<l>Aiyai, saying, ‘The turn [to supply] ghee for us is today’,</l>
<l>Having called out to her daughter,</l>
<l>The elderly lady [from] the middle-clan would arrive [at the scene],</l>
<l>Having come, carrying a churning-rope [and] a churning staff.</l>
      </lg>
    </div>
    <div rend="parallel">
    <p>
      <head type="subtitle">uraipāṭṭumaṭai </head>
    </p>
<p xml:lang="en">
  <head type="subtitle">An interval of song. </head>
</p>
  </div>
<div rend="parallel">
  <lg xml:id="cila17.2">
   <l>kuṭappā luṟaiyā kuviyimi lēṟṟiṉ</l>
<l>maṭakkaṇṇīr cōrum varuvatoṉ ṟuṇṭu</l>
<l>uṟinaṟu veṇṇe yurukā vurukum</l>
<l>maṟiteṟit tāṭā varuvatoṉ ṟuṇṭu</l>
<l>nāṉmulai yāya naṭuṅkupu niṉṟiraṅkum</l>
<l>māṉmaṇi vīḻum varuvatoṉṟuṇṭu</l>  
  </lg>
<lg xml:lang="en">
     <l>[Aiyai says]</l>
<l>The milk [in] the pot does not curdle. Innocent tears</l>
<l>Of the bull [with] a heap[-like] hump pour forth.</l>
<l>Something is coming.</l>
<l>The fragrant butter [on the pots suspended by] ropes</l>
<l>Melts without being made to melt. The goats</l>
<l>Do not play [anymore], jumping about. </l>
<l>Something is coming.</l>
<l>The herd of four-breasted [cows], shaking, stand [in one place],</l>
<l>Depressed. [Their] large bells fall off [their necks].</l>
<l>Something is coming.</l>     
      </lg>
</div>
    <div rend="parallel">
    <p>
      <head type="subtitle">karuppam. </head>
    </p>
<p xml:lang="en">
  <head type="subtitle"> The prognosis. </head>
</p>
  </div>
<div rend="parallel">
  <p xml:id="cila17.3">
    kuṭattuppā luṟaiyāmaiyum kuviyimilēṟṟiṉ maṭakkaṇṇīr cōrtalum 
    uṟiyilveṇṇe yurukāmaiyum maṟi muṭaṅki yāṭāmaiyum māṉmaṇi nilattaṟṟu vīḻtalum 
    varuvatōr tuṉpamuṇṭeṉa makaḷainōkki maṉamayaṅkātē maṇṇiṉ mātark kaṇiyākiya kaṇṇakiyun 
    tāṉkāṇa āyar pāṭiyileru maṉṟattu māyavaṉuṭaṉ tammuṉāṭiya vālacaritai nāṭakaṅkaḷil 
    vēṉeṭuṅkaṭ piññaiyōṭāṭiya kuravaiyāṭutum yāmeṉṟāḷ kaṟavaikaṉṟu tuyar nīṅkuka veṉavē
  </p>

  <p xml:lang="en">
  Saying, ‘The milk in the pot not curdling, the pouring forth of innocent tears by the bull [with] a heap[-like] hump,
the white butter [suspended in a pot by a] rope not melting, the goats, bending over, not playing, the great bell
thus falling to the ground, some distress is imminent,’ looking at [her] daughter, she [Aiyai] said, ‘Without being perturbed
[in] the mind, as Kaṇṇaki who is the [most] beautiful young lady on earth watches, we shall dance the Kuravai
that Piññai [with] spear[-like] long eyes danced in the dramatic passages in the Bālacarita that was danced
in front of us with Māyavaṉ upon the dung[-covered] village common, so that  misery may leave
the calves [of] the milk-cows.’
  </p>
</div>
